# Requests to try with VS Code's REST Client extension.
# Start the API first (npm start), then click Send Request above any request.
# The data lives in memory, so it starts fresh each time the API starts.

### Every show: 200
GET http://localhost:3100/shows

### One show: 200, Midnight Brass Band with 4 seats left
GET http://localhost:3100/shows/2

### A show that isn't there: 404
GET http://localhost:3100/shows/99

### Buy 2 tickets for show 2: 201, ticket 1 with total 66 (send it once, then ask for show 2 again)
POST http://localhost:3100/shows/2/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 2 }

### More tickets than are left: 409 (show 2 starts with 4 seats)
POST http://localhost:3100/shows/2/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 5 }

### A quantity that isn't a whole number from 1 to 8: 400
POST http://localhost:3100/shows/2/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": "two" }

### A refund for ticket 1: 204, and show 2 gets its seats back (buy ticket 1 first)
DELETE http://localhost:3100/tickets/1

### A ticket that isn't there: 404
DELETE http://localhost:3100/tickets/99
